== each img's image, natural size and border box, against Chromium's (tests/net/picture.chromium):
the same, img by img (22 of them)
== a source's width and height, its img's when it takes that source (tests/net/site/p/dims.html), against Chromium's (tests/net/picture-dims.chromium):
9 of 9 images the same
-- the declarations that sized them: the source's attributes, or the img's own
Id = both, P = width, X = declared('100px',written('width=100'),by('the source\'s width attribute'),in(author))
Id = both, P = height, X = declared('50px',written('height=50'),by('the source\'s height attribute'),in(author))
Id = wonly, P = width, X = declared('60px',written('width=60'),by('the source\'s width attribute'),in(author))
Id = wonly, P = height, X = initial(auto,'no declaration applies')
Id = nottaken, P = width, X = declared('40px',written('width=40'),by('the width attribute'),in(author))
Id = nottaken, P = height, X = initial(auto,'no declaration applies')
